ew military personnel nothing  compared to those who die or be forced  to flee because of the government's  harsh reaction one thing is certain that  was indeed the golden opportunity to  wipe out all the main opponents and more  in fact gulen was blamed as the  architect of the coup backed by the cia  quick parenthesis remember that the last  period of the war in syria had brought  relations between russia and turkey  closer together meeting with a lot of  criticism from the united states after  that a state of emergency was declared  and not only the sectors of the military  and civil service involved in the coup  were affected but also those with whom  in the previous 15 years of rule the  party had had to come to terms in order  to secure power i leave you with the  detailed account of the various arrests  and dismissals that followed at that  point this would have been the icing on  the cake to lay hands on the  constitution with reform and move the  country toward the strong  presidentialism inspired by the french  model the group had caused the main  opposition forces to express solidarity  with the president and show willingness  to consider their proposed  constitutional reform however the quorum  needed to pass the amendments wasn't  reached and it was appropriate to go  through a referendum on april 16 2017  erdogan won with just  51.41  a victory that among other things was  criticized both by domestic oppositions  which accused the government of  electoral fraud and by the organization  for security and cooperation in europe  and the council of europe it was an  outcome that reflected the deep internal  rift in the country where erdogan's  legitimacy was slowly being challenged  by a general climate of protest over  arrests and repression by the  authorities that went far beyond those  belonging to fetal aguilance  organization it was very difficult for  the oppositions to work because at the  first mistake they risked being branded  as gulenists which over time has become  synonymous with terrorists today's  turkey which will celebrate the 100th  anniversary of the birth of the republic  in 2023 has its leadership a president  far away from the figure the father of  the turks envisioned of the catalyst the  six arrows very few remain intact and  among them it's clear that secularism is  no longer among the features of the  turkish state but still the political  involution we are witnessing has been  countered by economic growth such that  the country has become a major regional  power that was at least until the most  recent monetary policies led to the  devaluation of the turkish lira  culminating in the currency crisis of  2021 and the consequent rise in  inflation generating the risk of  stagnation in the economy due to the  rising cost of living and falling  internal demand all of this would also  impact the degree of discontent so much  so that impulse approval ratings toward  the erdogan's actions would have dropped  from 55.8 percent in march 2020 to 38.6  at the end of 2021 the lowest percentage  in recent years even lower than in early  2019 when dissatisfaction with the  performance of the economy had caused  the erdogan to lose control of istanbul  and ankara in local elections but it's  good to stop here for today i thank you  all for your attention and i will see  you in the next video ciao
 

